    <!-- DACS 2.7 -->
    <bioghist>
      <head>Historical Note</head>
      <p>The history of the Old Dominion Chrysanthemum Society was written by its Chairman, Joan
        Seeger, in 1994.</p>
      <p>On March 19, 1960, a small group of Northern Virginia gardeners, members of the Falls
        Church Garden Club and interested in Chrysanthemum culture, met and organized as a branch of
        Potomac Chrysanthemum Society.</p>
    </bioghist>
    <!-- DACS 3.1 -->
    <scopecontent>
      <head>Scope and Content</head>
      <p>The Old Dominion Chrysanthemum Society archive from 1959 to 1994 consists of the following
        documents: Minutes, Newsletters, Memos, Photos, Reports, Public Notices, Architectural
        Archaeological Comments, Programs, Minutes, and Correspondence, etc. </p>
      <p>The archive is organized as follows: <list>
          <item>Series 1: Falls Church Garden Club</item>
          <item>Series 2: Old Dominion Branch </item>
          <item>Series 3: Old Dominion Chrysanthemum Society Newsletters</item>
          <item>Series 4: Annual Chrysanthemum Show</item>
          <item>Series 5: Executive Board &amp; Monthly Meeting Minutes</item>
          <item>Series 6: Certificate</item>
          <item>Series 7: Constitution</item>
          <item>Series 8: Tax Status</item>
          <item>Series 9: Chrysanthemum Show</item>
          <item>Series 10: Awards</item>
          <item>Series 11: Directory </item>
        </list>
      </p>
    </scopecontent>
